{
 "plan": {
  "title": "District Health Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Comparing key health indicators across districts",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Children 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"Children age 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)\" AS vacc_rate FROM district_health_factsheet WHERE \"Source\" = 'District factsheet' ORDER BY vacc_rate DESC",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "vacc_rate"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Children under 5 years who are stunted (%)",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"Children under 5 years who are stunted (%)\" AS stunted_rate FROM district_health_factsheet WHERE \"Source\" = 'District factsheet' ORDER BY stunted_rate DESC",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "stunted_rate"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Women age 15-49 years who are literate (%)",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"Women age 15-49 years who are literate (%)\" AS literacy_rate FROM district_health_factsheet WHERE \"Source\" = 'District factsheet' ORDER BY literacy_rate DESC",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "literacy_rate"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Institutional births (%)",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", \"Institutional births (%)\" AS institutional_rate FROM district_health_factsheet WHERE \"Source\" = 'District factsheet' ORDER BY institutional_rate DESC",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "institutional_rate"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard presents four key health indicators for each district, allowing a quick visual comparison. {{p1}} shows the percentage of children aged 12-23 months who are fully vaccinated, highlighting districts with higher immunization coverage. {{p2}} displays the stunting rate among children under five, identifying areas with greater nutritional challenges. {{p3}} reveals literacy rates among women aged 15-49, indicating educational attainment levels. Finally, {{p4}} measures institutional birth rates, reflecting access to healthcare services during childbirth. Together, these panels provide a comprehensive snapshot of district-level health performance."
 },
